<title>USA: Dynasil sets two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>Dynasil sets two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>WEST BERLIN, N.J. 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dynasil Corp said Monday that its board has set a two-for-one stock split.</p>
<p>Shareholders of record on October 1 will be issued one additional share of Dynasil common; settlement is November 1, the company said.</p>
<p>Dynasil, which makes synthetic parts for the semiconductor and optical components industry, said new shares should be mailed on October 30.</p>
<p>The company had 1.1 million shares outstanding at the end of the company's third quarter on June 30.</p>
